<%/* A visual the agent is still writing, while its words stream: its block's
     tag is in (so Prelude knows it's a flow or a map) but not its closing
     fence. A placeholder stands where it will be, rather than its lines
     growing as code, and the words after it keep coming once the block
     closes. Each push renders the message afresh, so the drawn visual (or,
     if it can't be read, the block and why) takes this one's place.
     `it.of` is 'flow' or 'map'. */%>
<figure class="stack gap-2" aria-busy="true">
  <span class="skeleton block" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <figcaption class="muted"><%= it.of === 'map' ? 'Drawing a map of the parts…' : 'Drawing a flow…' %></figcaption>
</figure>
